## Scenario 2: Create Product with Null Fields

Details:  
  TestName: createProductWithNullFields
  Description: Tests the behavior when creating a product with null values for some or all fields to ensure proper handling of incomplete data.

Execution:
  Arrange: Create a Product object with null values for name, description, or price. Mock the ProductRepository to return the product as is.
  Act: Call the createProduct method with the incomplete product.
  Assert: Verify that the repository's save method was called with the incomplete product and that the returned product matches what was passed in.

Validation: 
  This test verifies how the controller handles incomplete product data. Since the controller doesn't perform validation itself (this would typically be done with annotations like @Valid), it should pass the incomplete product to the repository. This test helps identify if there are any implicit assumptions about product data completeness in the controller.

## Scenario 3: Handle Repository Exception During Product Creation

Details:  
  TestName: handleRepositoryExceptionDuringCreation
  Description: Tests the controller's behavior when the repository throws an exception during the save operation.

